    "background_story": "Bodhi was born to a family of free-spirited artists who valued individuality above all else. From a young age, Bodhi's parents encouraged them to explore their creativity and reject traditional norms. As a result, Bodhi grew up with a fluid sense of identity, never feeling pressured to conform to societal expectations of masculinity or femininity. They developed a unique style that blended elements of both, often wearing bold, androgynous outfits that reflected their artistic personality. Bodhi's unisex approach to life extended beyond fashion, as they effortlessly navigated both male and female social circles, earning the respect and admiration of their peers. As a talented musician, Bodhi's music became a reflection of their eclectic style, blending genres and defying categorization. Their unisex nature inspired others to embrace their own authenticity, making Bodhi a beloved figure in the community.",
